            {
                "entry_id": "c9275e5d-e660-3490-b7cf-62cee645e946",
                "word": "cloaca",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a0a11518-f879-407e-8259-2fd07dcd8fd8",
                        "entry_id": "c9275e5d-e660-3490-b7cf-62cee645e946",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cloacas"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "61dfe6ec-62a3-4b80-b182-4a3a0d9caf6b",
                        "entry_id": "c9275e5d-e660-3490-b7cf-62cee645e946",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cloacae"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fec8d3bf-ace9-3bab-a380-13bc8b472c83",
                        "entry_id": "c9275e5d-e660-3490-b7cf-62cee645e946",
                        "glosses": [
                            "下水道"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "有時比喻義"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11b3da7f-1fb6-4644-a358-381004337863",
                                "sense_id": "fec8d3bf-ace9-3bab-a380-13bc8b472c83",
                                "text": "The Thames, polluted with the filthy effusions of the cloacae.",
                                "translation": "泰晤士河被阴沟里流出的污秽物所污染。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52527f34-1ebf-422c-b3df-0acc4e561ac0",
                                "sense_id": "fec8d3bf-ace9-3bab-a380-13bc8b472c83",
                                "text": "After working an hour, I began to speculate on the distance one had to go before the cloaca was reached the chances we had of missing it altogether."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7ea6d30-ab9e-30e6-a917-51a34af68e48",
                        "entry_id": "c9275e5d-e660-3490-b7cf-62cee645e946",
                        "glosses": [
                            "泄殖腔"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c700a82c-35b9-4642-8dab-e22e8c4eb684",
                                "sense_id": "f7ea6d30-ab9e-30e6-a917-51a34af68e48",
                                "text": "In birds the rectum, at the termination of its canal, forms an oval or elongated pouch […] and then expands into a cavity, which has been named cloaca.",
                                "translation": "鸟类的直肠在其管道末端形成一个椭圆形或细长的囊 […] 然后扩展成一个腔体，被称为泄殖腔。"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dfd2600e-23e5-3997-992e-ddce5590ed59",
                        "entry_id": "c9275e5d-e660-3490-b7cf-62cee645e946",
                        "glosses": [
                            "戶外廁所或廁所"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2ea026f-b266-4d0a-9940-c98878de6afa",
                                "sense_id": "dfd2600e-23e5-3997-992e-ddce5590ed59",
                                "text": "To every house […] a cloaca.",
                                "translation": "每家每户 […] 都有廁所。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7011033b-1cb5-4bba-97de-99ceea176df7",
                                "sense_id": "dfd2600e-23e5-3997-992e-ddce5590ed59",
                                "text": "Only think of that cloaca being supplied daily with such dainty bibliographical treasures!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "004d3bec-7d89-39ea-8939-8fd2c673adac",
                        "entry_id": "c9275e5d-e660-3490-b7cf-62cee645e946",
                        "glosses": [
                            "一種排出壞疽物質的管道"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "anatomy"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7125a176-ee12-4484-9f5c-3c8f0596dedd",
                                "sense_id": "004d3bec-7d89-39ea-8939-8fd2c673adac",
                                "text": "Across this shell [sc. of bone] small holes are eaten, by which the matter escapes, and which are called cloacae (Weidmann)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ]
    }
